---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Pricing" description="qyl is free: the Collector, the hosted MCP endpoint, the qyl plugin and the local MCP server.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="site-shell pricing-shell">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">One plan · every shipped feature</span>
        <h1 class="page-title">qyl is free.</h1>
        <p class="lede">No feature matrix and no pretend enterprise tier. Run the Collector yourself, or connect your agent to the hosted endpoint once your account has a Collector project there.</p>
      </div>
      <article class="pricing-card" aria-labelledby="free-plan">
        <div class="pricing-card__head">
          <span>Everything included</span>
          <div class="price"><strong>€0</strong><small>today</small></div>
        </div>
        <div class="pricing-card__body">
          <ul class="check-list">
            <li>The Collector: OTLP trace, log and metric ingestion, storage and analysis</li>
            <li>The local stdio MCP server</li>
            <li>Hosted MCP endpoint for accounts with a Collector project: every tool, plus MCP Events for new error traces</li>
            <li>The qyl plugin for Claude Code and Codex</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="button button--light" href="/docs/getting-started/" id="free-plan">Install qyl</a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="editorial-section editorial-section--raised">
    <div class="site-shell section-intro">
      <div><span class="eyebrow">The plain answer</span><h2 class="section-title">No billing system is hidden behind this page.</h2></div>
      <p class="lede">One developer built all of it using Anthropic and OpenAI models to the fullest. If pricing ever changes, the terms and limits will be published before anyone is charged. The local Collector works without a hosted account.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
